From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 05:45:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07786/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter7: fix hazard LOS
 checked on wrong axis in omni mode (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5880)

Synthetic probe of HazardAwareNavWorldModel.is_lethal (live-reachable via
arc_hazard_pruner -> arc_loop_solve) found _charge_unobstructed always checked
wall line-of-sight along the single fitted self.hazard_axis, but omni-mode
chargers charge along their OWN per-charger facing axis. A vertical charger with
a wall on its column had its shielding checked on the row axis -> wall missed ->
safe move flagged lethal -> over-pruning the winning path.
Fix: _charge_unobstructed takes a per-charge axis; is_lethal checks LOS on each
charge's true travel axis. tu93 L3 calibration stays CLEAN (FN=0 FP=0
win_path_pruned=0; real game has both row- and col-facing chargers). 28 nav+
hazard tests pass + new regression test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
